      "writtenOn": "2023-03-03T15:48:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ray,\nThanks for pointing to this CL in b/271481061#comment2.\nThis approach only works for decoders. With this change isFormatSupported() works as expected for decoders, but it still fails for encoders.\n\nFor an encoder that advertises support for CBR, isFormatSupported() still returns fail when bitrate-mode is set to CBR in the format.\nSome details in b/270272952#comment14 and beyond.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "3f57fbd2f7b34c84133f35316d20c9142daf1e61",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "19b1a5ca_9477c290",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1981835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-03T16:21:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From what you said seems like this patch, regardless of whether the API is modified or not, fixes isFormatSupported() only for decoders but there is still unresolved issue with encoders in CBR mode?",
      "parentUuid": "f820fcb9_c5d50feb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "3f57fbd2f7b34c84133f35316d20c9142daf1e61",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "67c5fad7_8c7a6922",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1047003
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-03T18:24:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. That is what I saw in my tests (Though I did not use this CL, but a similar approach).\nReason is createFromProfileLevel() seems to creating default capabilties and not based on what is in the xml. Thus even when the encoder advertises CBR, it wasn\u0027t getting reflected in the capabilities created.",
      "parentUuid": "19b1a5ca_9477c290",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "3f57fbd2f7b34c84133f35316d20c9142daf1e61",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7efb156e_8ed7b2ea",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1981835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-03T19:22:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for clarification. If this issue is already known to your team and someone is working on the fix then it\u0027s ok for me to abandon this CL and wait for the final solution. From my perspective, it\u0027s even better not to have to deal with the API release, since I am not familiar with required process. Your confirmation that such approach is correct for decoder is enough for me to handle this internally until final patch is ready. Please let me know the way you prefer.",
      "parentUuid": "67c5fad7_8c7a6922",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "3f57fbd2f7b34c84133f35316d20c9142daf1e61",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f0e0cb38_61671131",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1089769
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-06T13:19:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I found the current approach regresses decoders as well (b/276697204#comment2): \"secure-playback\" decoder feature is not reflected in the caps created by createFromProfileLevel(), and hence the logic starts failing to find secure decoders.\n\n\nMy feeling is that isFormatSupported() should not use createFromProfileLevel() at all... and instead create a full copy of the caps (with only profile/level modified).",
      "parentUuid": "7efb156e_8ed7b2ea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "3f57fbd2f7b34c84133f35316d20c9142daf1e61",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
